<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Multi-Fractal

A ''pattern integrity'': an entity reads not as a single thing but as a ''container that binds many scope-bound instances of ONE primitive'' — and each instance can itself stand as a container. That last clause separates //fractal// from merely //plural//: the shape recurses.

The house keeps standing in this shape at every plane. Name it once; recognize it everywhere.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/instances>>

!! The Five Instances (PENTADIC)

| Plane | The many | Bound by | One primitive |
|---|---|---|---|
| ''memory'' | verbatim · ast · form · mesh palaces | the mempalace root | one ChromaDB engine |
| ''l-space'' | the Voices/Syād atlas of charts | the colorless active center (`ha.ka.ba` hub) | one manifold |
| ''identity'' | the handle-Circle constellation | the "me" Circle | one mutual binding (the Circle is the //closure//, not a central group) |
| ''vessel'' | the `#has`-cap-stack | `composeVessel` | one cap-module |
| ''mesh'' | Lararium · Nexus · DreamNet | a re-anchoring the mesh records and never specifies | one delegation edge |

Five instances, no sixth straining for room (#PENTA_1). A cluster that demands a sixth signals a regrounding, never an extension.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/laws>>

!! The Two Laws That Make It Load-Bearing

''1 — the container holds private (no-global-X).'' Every container above joins //local-first//: the mempalace never federates, the l-space chart stays provisional-not-territory, the "me" Circle discloses only by choosing. So the integrity carries ''"no global now" into every plane'' — no global memory, no global chart, no global self. The container is always the private join. <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/causal-islands>>

''2 — the instances may OVERLAP, held apart by sovereignty (substrate ≠ sovereignty).'' The instances do not partition cleanly — a single substrate (one device, one palace dir, one chart-point) may sit under several containers at once. The structure reads as an ''overlapping set-cover (a hypergraph), never a tree.'' What keeps the overlap from fusing the containers: each instance carries its own ''sovereignty'' (its own key, log, scope) over the ''shared substrate''. The overlap stays safe only because the per-instance sovereignty stays distinct — the same law the causal-island doctrine rules for co-located vessels, now read at every fractal.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/test>>

!! The Test

A candidate structure stands as multi-fractal when ALL hold:
* one primitive recurs across the many (never N bespoke shapes);
* a container binds them, and the container joins ''private/local-first'';
* an instance may itself contain instances (the recursion clause);
* instances MAY share substrate, held apart by distinct sovereignty;
* the natural count lands bounded near five (#PENTA_1).

A structure that merges the instances into ONE shared graph (sovereignty fused, not just substrate) fails the test — that reads as the Matrix anti-pattern (planes bled), never multi-fractal. <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/mookuauhau>>

<<~/ahu>>

