<<~ ahu #/why-it-recurses>>

!! Why it recurses ~ each rung answers a capture the rung below cannot

The shape above says the recursion happens. This says WHY it must.

''Capture requires a counterparty that can act ALONE.'' A lone veil falls to whoever holds the vessel; a lone dyad to whoever holds the device; a lone person to their host; a lone realm to a patron-realm. At each scale the cure is the same move — ''a mutual hold with something that cannot act alone'' — and that hold IS the next scale.

''So the cure at scale N is the constructor at scale N+1.'' The ladder never was a taxonomy of sizes. It reads as a chain of mutual protections, each rung existing because the rung below can be disposed of by one hand.

''Which is why the top MUST NOT close.'' Follow the pattern one step past the last rung and it says what no rung can: a closed top would be ''the thing that can act alone over everything'', and every scale beneath it capturable by it. A closed top is an empire — by arithmetic, never by taste. So DreamNet stands as the FIELD that Nexuses found //within//, recognition edges stay NON-TRANSITIVE, and the fractal terminates nowhere.

''Read per-AXIS, never up one ladder'' (`dreamnet-architecture#two-axis-topology`): the two axes form //a 2D coordinate plane, never a single ladder// and //they never nest//. The capture-and-cure chain runs along each axis independently — which is also why delegation //tops at the cabal; above it, treaty// (`lararium-identity#five-scale`). The social axis already refuses to close on its own grounds.

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation#/the-constructor>>

